# Bare enum value carried by two named enums: game rejects as ambiguous, LSP silently takes the first

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

Found by the B046 lane, 2026-08-30, via live game probe. Pre-existing and
unrelated to B046, which merely adds two enums to the pool that can collide.

## Defect
When a bare value name is carried by more than one NAMED enum, the game
refuses to compile it:

    Found multiple matching enum values

Confirmed against the live game (Trackmania + Openplanet 1.29.5) on `Turbo`,
`WallJump` and `FreeWheeling`.

The LSP takes the first match and says nothing. That is a false NEGATIVE — the
tool stays silent on code the game will reject. Less damaging than a false
positive, but it is the LSP failing at its job, and the failure is invisible
until the plugin is compiled in-game.

## Why it matters more than the raw count suggests
Many engine value names are already multiply defined, so the population is not
small. It also inverts an assumption the resolver leans on elsewhere: that
finding A match is finding THE match. Anywhere the index resolves a bare value
by first-hit, the same silent-wrong-answer shape can appear — including hover
and go-to-definition, which would point at an arbitrary one of the candidates.

## Work
- Probe first, as B044 and B046 both did: enumerate bare value names carried by
  two or more named enums, submit them to the game, and confirm the rejection
  is uniform rather than dependent on the enums involved. Do not infer this
  from the dump.
- Then decide the diagnostic: an ambiguity ERROR matching the game, naming the
  candidate enums so the fix (qualify it) is obvious.
- Check hover and go-to-definition for the same first-hit assumption and make
  them agree with whatever the resolver decides.
- Distinguish carefully from ANONYMOUS enum collisions, which B044 already
  settled — the game rejects those for a different reason (the name is
  unspellable, not ambiguous) and the message differs.

## Gate
FP fixture ERROR counts WILL rise if any fixture uses an ambiguous bare value,
and that rise is the fix working. Every new error must be shown to be a name
the game genuinely rejects as ambiguous — verified by probe, name by name, not
assumed. Measure two binaries on the same machine at the same time (baselines
14/1485, 5/276, 2/35, 4/2, 4/4).

## Related
B046 (found it; adds `ESceneCharVisNotice` and `ESceneVehicleVisEvent` to the
collidable pool, documented inline in its new fixture and in
`todo-false-positives.txt`), B044 (anonymous-enum value names — the adjacent
but distinct case), B016, B052 (the other resolution-accuracy gap B046 found
and declined to fix), B007.
